// A brace group in VALUE position whose entry has no `: value` and is not a bare field name. The
// map-entry rule rejects it — it does not accept it and complain afterwards, which is what would
// consume the braces and break the block fallback in a match arm (see
// `control_flow/match_block_arm_single_call.noe`). Rejecting still lets the rule carry its own
// reason, so here, where no block alternative exists to win instead, the pointed message surfaces
// rather than the raw expected-set wall.
// expect: error E0003 at 9:7
// expect: exit 1
x = { "a" };
